{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:Observations.DoubleSlitQPhase","@type":"LeanModule","name":"Observations.DoubleSlitQPhase","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.double_slit_q_phase_diff_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.double_slit_q_phase_diff_classical","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/double-slit-q-phase.lean#L44-L48","doc":"At q = 1, the phase difference reduces to the standard Young formula. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.double_slit_q_phase_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.double_slit_q_phase_classical","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/double-slit-q-phase.lean#L39-L42","doc":"At q = 1, the q-phase reduces to the geometric phase. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.double_slit_q_phase_diff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.double_slit_q_phase_diff","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/double-slit-q-phase.lean#L32-L37","doc":"The q-deformed phase difference between two slit paths.\nΔΦ_q = q⁻¹ · (2πd sin θ / λ) + (1 − q⁻¹) · Δφ_ξ ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Experimental.double_slit_q_phase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Experimental.double_slit_q_phase","kind":"def","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/double-slit-q-phase.lean#L23-L30","doc":"The q-deformed path phase along a path through a slit.\nΦ_q = q⁻¹ · Φ_geom + (1 − q⁻¹) · Φ_Reeb.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:double-slit-q-phase}`\nRef: [leitner2026] Chapter 6, §Double-slit experiment ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:double-slit-q-phase","label":"def:double-slit-q-phase","md":"quantum-observable-universe/observations/double-slit-q-phase.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}